WEBVTT

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.410
"Giant Explosion in the City"
"Recurrence of the Lost Phenomenon?"

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.290
Early this morning, there was a great
explosion in the south eastern area of Tokyo.
"Giant Explosion in the City"
"Recurrence of the Lost Phenomenon?"

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.580
After three years, could this
be a recurrence of the Lost?
"Giant Explosion in the City"
"Recurrence of the Lost Phenomenon?"

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.910
Currently, we have no reports of any deaths.
"Giant Explosion in the City"
"Recurrence of the Lost Phenomenon?"

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.120
For your safety, please do not travel
outside unless absolutely necessary.
"Giant Explosion in the City"
"Recurrence of the Lost Phenomenon?"

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.200
I repeat...
"Giant Explosion in the City"
"Recurrence of the Lost Phenomenon?"

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.370
Whoa, seriously?

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.160
We should be grateful that it
happened in the lock-down district...

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.620
Everyone, go and support
the officers in the precinct!

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.580
There not enough people to get
a full grasp of the situation.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.870
Great job everyone.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.500
Negishi, aren't you off-duty today?

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.660
I'm going to borrow Syunpei for a bit.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:45.910
Huh? Me?

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:46.830
"Lost 1" "Lost 2" "Lost 3"
Huh? Me?

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.330
"Lost 1" "Lost 2" "Lost 3"
Negishi!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.250
"Lost 1" "Lost 2" "Lost 3"

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.040
Takuya! Takuya!

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.000
"AFTERLOST"

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:40.040
"Episode 4: Suspicion"

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.910
Takuya...

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.250
You two were the ones who put him
up to this! Telling him to go to Lost!

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.950
What the hell are Tama-Shi!

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.700
You two knew, right?!

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.950
Takuya might die!

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.080
How are you gonna take responsibility?!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.790
Geek... you should go into hiding.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.580
Huh? Why?!

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.660
I'm sure they already know you
infiltrated the lock-down district.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.830
If you stay out in the public,
the police will come knocking.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:22.370
Even if you tell me something like that...

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.830
Then, come to my place.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.660
It's not that I'm trying to redeem myself.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.500
But my place is a good place to hide.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.120
"Examination Room"

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.450
You should come as well.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.500
Let's go.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.250
Decide for yourself.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:51.330
This is... This is the result of your actions.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.410
Excuse us.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:07.500
I am Negishi, from the
first division of investigations.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.080
I am Aoyama.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.250
Can we help you?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:15.580
Are you a victim of the second
Lost that occurred this morning?

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.620
What makes you think that?

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.120
And I believe that phenomenon
was different from the Lost.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:24.450
Well, that's what the public calls it, anyways.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.910
Please take a look at this.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.370
This was taken from a camera
within the lock-down district.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.580
There is no mistake that this
young lady is the one in the image.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.040
This gentleman...

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:39.500
He is in the intensive care unit
and cannot have visitors.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.290
I feel bad for him, but it seems like
he merely reaped what he sowed.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.580
What were the two of you doing
in the lock-down district?

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:51.040
My apologies. It seems they trespassed
the district in the middle of their date.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.540
Aren't you a high school student?
What school do you go to?

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.540
Do you have your school ID?

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:01.870
This girl lost her family
three years ago during the Lost.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:06.200
She has not attended school
since then and stays at my home.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.580
Of course, we make sure she still studies.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:11.080
But she still goes on dates.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.620
Why not? A change of pace is good sometimes.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.540
You don't look well. Are you eating all right?

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.540
Miss Ryoko, you're just letting them go?

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.080
I bet you're not popular with girls.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.040
Huh? What do you mean by that?

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:37.080
Why can't we tell them the truth?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.790
The Agency is very large.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:43.200
Their supporters have infiltrated
all parts of the government.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.160
That includes the police.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:50.500
Huh? This is your home?

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:53.120
It's a bit too big for a single man.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.750
Please come in.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.700
Negishi's special <i>mirin </i>rice!

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.200
Help yourself if you want seconds!

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.120
For some reason, the taste is really addictive.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.000
Y-Yeah...

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:13.540
I don't know what the two of you are secretly
looking into, but learn from her well.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:16.080
--I hate to admit it, but there's a reason
she's lieutenant at such a young age.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.910
--Here!
--I hate to admit it, but there's a reason
she's lieutenant at such a young age.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:22.200
As expected of the daughter of
a legendary police officer, huh?

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.450
Souma.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.370
How admirable.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:31.200
Suzuna!

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.950
How did you find us?

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.700
So, you came to finish us off.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:40.410
I can erase you easily at any time. Him, too.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.700
You said something strange last time.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.160
That it wouldn't be good to
overwrite things any further.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.790
What did you mean?

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.040
Let me give you a piece of useful information.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.950
Well then, I will make this car disappear!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:09.330
Now... One...! Two...! Three!

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.500
Amazing!

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:19.330
That was Mr. Yoshiaki, a magician that
is recently gaining a lot of popularity!

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.120
--Who are you?

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.330
--Hot! Hot! Hot!
--Who are you?

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.870
Hidaka Keigo of the Hidaka Detective Agency?

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.370
A detective?

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:55.660
I've been looking into a certain
institution for children for many years.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:58.540
The Light of Hope Academy for the Handicapped.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:03.580
I've already confirmed that you attended there.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:08.040
So? Do you plan to sell that information
to a magazine? Help yourself.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:10.700
No, no. I have no interest in money.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:13.080
Actually, I want to help you.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:19.450
Mr. Yoshiaki. You're searching for your
long-lost big brother, aren't you?

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:22.250
You were both raised in the same institution.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.450
His name was Tsubasa, right?

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:28.330
I'm sure you'd get a lot of response
if you called out to him publicly on TV.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:31.450
And you'd get more viewers, too.

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:37.410
But, unfortunately, you can't do that.
The reason why is because your big brother...

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:40.620
So you know that much.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:41.830
"Yoshiaki"

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.000
"Yoshiaki"
How about funding me 500,000 yen?

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.120
So it's about money, after all.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.750
Well I have to get a little.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.870
Hey, hear me out a bit...

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.250
Ow! Ow! Ow! OW!

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.580
Are you racketeering again, Mr. Keigo?

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:58.830
Wait! You're wrong! You're wrong, Ryoko!

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:07.120
A civil servant would never understand
the sorrows of a freelancer.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:11.870
Who was the one who went freelance because
being a civil servant was too stuffy?

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:16.870
So, the reason you came to me...

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:19.290
Has there been some kind of development?

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:25.790
I still don't know if the Agency is involved,
but there's a man I'd like you to look into.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:30.330
He's a freelance courier, but it seems he
used to be in the same profession as you.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.830
I've met him somewhere before...

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.910
Really?! Then, please look into it, sir!

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:39.290
I can't turn down a request from you.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.370
But, don't be reckless.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.790
You, too, Mr. Keigo.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.870
She's such a slave driver.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:56.540
She's just like you.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:04.580
Takuya!

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:06.870
Yumiko.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.120
Where's Kouta?

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:12.660
I looked for him everywhere after
what happened, but I couldn't find him.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:15.660
Then, the second Lost happened...

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:21.660
Where's Yuki?!

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.910
It's okay. She's somewhere safe.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.160
I see.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:34.040
Oh, that's right. Yumiko, do you
know a producer named Seiji?

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:37.250
Huh? Why do you know about him, Takuya?

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:44.620
"Seiji, the producer of SPR5, dies in accident.
Was falling asleep while driving the cause?"

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:48.700
It was breaking news just a moment ago.
He fell asleep while driving.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:54.540
No way. He was my clue to Lost.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:12:01.250
Hey... don't go to Lost anymore.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:08.080
I can't stand watching you get hurt anymore.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.750
There's no guarantee that
you'll come back alive.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.830
Thank you, Yumiko.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.620
But I have to fulfill the contract.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:26.580
Sorry for barging in so suddenly.
I made lunch boxes.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:32.450
Let's eat them together.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:35.040
Well, thank you for the food.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.830
It's not bad.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:45.540
Unfortunately, I'm out of <i>mirin </i>today.
It's normally more delicious.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:52.290
Your father was an amazing person, Yuki.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.000
Not at all.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:56.160
The authority on applied physics.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:59.080
The director of Japan's research institute.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:04.250
That's amazing. I was an arts student so
I have no idea about subjects like that.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:10.080
My dad was also involved in the Lost.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.950
Day after day. Work. Work.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:16.750
I knew that being a
police officer was hard work.

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:20.620
Even so, I was lonely.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:24.750
Have a safe trip.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:27.750
Got it. I'll be back soon. Yeah.

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:34.040
Weren't we going to the
amusement park tomorrow?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.370
How many broken promises now?

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.950
I'm sick of this.

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:44.120
Souma, father is working
hard for everyone's future.

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.910
"Toshima Park"
Be more patient.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:46.870
"Toshima Park"

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:57.000
In the end, I still admired my dad.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:01.290
I wanted to become an
amazing officer, just like him.

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:08.290
That's why, when he was caught in the Lost,
I was more frustrated than sad.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:17.450
I followed my dad and became a police officer,
but then he just suddenly disappeared.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:23.910
It's been three years since the Lost and
there are a lot of people who've given up...

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:29.290
...but I won't.

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:32.580
I believe my father is alive.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:34.660
"YUKI I AM WAITING AT LOST"

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:55.830
It's delicious.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:14.410
What's going on, Ma'am? Isn't this a
research facility owned by Lacuna?

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:15.290
Well, then...

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:22.580
Um... will you listen to my story?

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:25.700
I want you to know, Miss Ryoko.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:29.540
Where I was and what was done to me.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:32.330
Unforgivable.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.660
Jeez...

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:45.910
I apologize for the wait.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:52.580
I am responsible for the public
relations of Lacuna Chemical.

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:55.160
I am Negishi, from the
first division of investigations.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.450
I am Aoyama.

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.750
What brings you here today?

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:04.950
I heard there was a burglary
at this facility the other day.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:11.080
We have already reported the incident
to the police. Was there a problem?

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:14.910
May I take a look inside the facility?

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:19.370
My apologies. We have a
responsibility for confidentiality.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.660
Of course, we would fully cooperate
if you have a search warrant...

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:34.410
Come in.

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.370
Excuse me.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:38.200
A guest?

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:40.370
The police came by for questioning.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:46.000
I don't believe there is a problem, but she
may have encountered the test subject.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.330
Oh?

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:50.000
How long do you plan to leave her be?

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.120
Look what's become of Souma.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:55.910
The older sister has a more potential.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:17:00.620
She was able to create a Lost-like
phenomenon without using an artifact.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:04.080
It'll be interesting to let
her roam free for a while.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:10.200
I will eliminate her if she becomes an
obstacle to our plans. Please be aware.

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:12.370
So harsh.

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:14.830
Please put a limit to your curiosity.

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:23.660
You idiot! Don't get involved in that area!

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.330
Got it? This is an order from our superiors.

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:30.700
Don't make me repeat myself again.
You're always causing so much trouble!

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:32.660
<i>That </i>area?

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:36.000
I can't protect you more than this.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:40.160
By the way, I was dragged around
with no idea of what's going on...

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.500
Shut up. Get back to your post.

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:45.330
Uh... Yes.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:47.330
See, what did I tell you?

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:49.620
The police is an organization, too.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.620
I'm sure of it now.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:57.660
Pressure is usually applied
when you get closer to the truth.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:59.290
Give it up!

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:02.290
"Lacuna Chemical = the Agency"

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:06.660
Finally. I think I'll be able
to chase after my Dad.

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.200
And...

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:12.750
Unforgivable.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:16.410
Thank you for telling me.

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:19.790
It must have been hard for you, Yuki.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:24.410
I'll be sure to drag the
Agency out into the public.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.620
I made a promise.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:40.000
Oh, excuse...

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.540
Wait, Takuya?!

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:44.660
Oh, Yuki.

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:48.080
Takuya, are you all right?

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:48.830
No problem.

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.540
Of course there is!

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:52.580
Well, let's go.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.410
Found it.

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:01.750
It was him, after all.

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:06.500
Ryoko, your instincts are amazing.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:10.910
"Danger Restricted Access"

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:17.200
Please give me a break.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:19.950
What's the point of searching
through real estate documents?

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:25.000
Before the Lost, a certain factory
site was put up for sale.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:28.040
Lacuna Chemical also put in a bid for it.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:32.040
They announced their plans to make
it a second research facility.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:36.330
But wasn't the highest
bidder Sugisawa Industries?

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:40.080
Yes. In the end, they were caught
in the Lost and disappeared.

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:45.290
Lucky for Lacuna. A huge loss
for Sugisawa Industries.

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:46.700
Found it!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.580
The contract!

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:53.620
The highest bidder was Lacuna Chemical,
but they retracted their bid?

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:58.450
In the end, the second largest bidder,
Sugisawa Industries, bought the land?

00:19:58.450 --> 00:20:01.620
It's weird that they retracted
their bid after winning out.

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:05.870
The date... It was right before the Lost!

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:12.200
In other words, the Agency knew when the
Lost would happen and how big it'd be!

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:15.870
I've finally caught them!
Hey, let's take this document and--

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:36.160
Jeez, that's why he told you not
to sniff around anymore, Ma'am.

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:39.330
You're part of the Agency...

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:42.870
You know, I really took a liking to you.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:47.500
But can I say one thing? The <i>mirin </i>rice.

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:52.330
It tastes like shit. Seriously.

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.750
Great job.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:11.000
You wanted to talk?

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.870
Things are hard on you, too.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:17.750
You finally escaped the Agency, but then
killed your brother with your own hands.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:21.580
But, that's not the case.

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:28.830
Let me give you a piece of useful information.

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:32.500
Yuki's brother, Souma...

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:33.790
He's still alive.

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:42.080
Souma is...

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:47.080
As long as you head toward Lost,
he'll appear again.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:50.660
You'll have to fight your little brother.

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:58.620
Are you prepared for that?
If not, don't involve Takuya any further.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:05.700
I want... to save Souma.

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:38.000
"AFTERLOST"

00:23:43.750 --> 00:23:46.290
Next Episode: "Affection."
